    fit: 'You like ambiguous problems and are willing to keep one skill genuinely current every year, not just once — see <a href="/blog/career-options/is-data-science-a-good-career-in-india">is data science a good career in India</a> for the full breakdown of who this fits.',
    caution: 'The shortage is real, and so is entry-level saturation for anyone without a shipped, explainable project to show for it.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Consulting & advisory',
    pills: [
      { axis: 'Income ceiling', level: 'High', tone: 'good' },
      { axis: 'Security', level: 'Medium', tone: 'mid' },
      { axis: 'Growth', level: 'High', tone: 'good' },
      { axis: 'AI-resilience', level: 'Med-High', tone: 'good' },
      { axis: 'Life-fit demand', level: 'High', tone: 'caution' },
    ],
    reality:
      'Senior consulting and advisory pay stretches well past Rs 50 lakh at experienced levels, with client-facing judgment work holding up better against automation than the research and slide-production layer underneath it.',
