    note: 'A high income-ceiling career with a high life-fit demand — consulting, sales, senior IT — will fight your wiring for years if the demand level genuinely does not suit you.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Context',
    body: 'How much runway — money, family support, dependents — do you have to absorb a lower-income stretch while you build toward a specialisation that raises your ceiling? Or does your situation need income now, which should push you toward a bucket that already scores well on security and pay today?',
    note: 'Context decides the order you chase these axes in. It does not decide which axes matter — all five still matter, just not all at the same time.',
